@* The container of the map's own controls (the attribution (i), 03 section 4.4): empty on purpose, like EdgeBubbles. MapLibre builds its control container inside the
   element it draws into, and that element must come last in the Location page so that the keyboard reaches the map canvas after the right stack (01 section 10.2:
   attribution, bubbles, recenter, layers, canvas). realmMap.js therefore moves the control container here once the map exists; the attribution then comes before the
   bubbles and the right stack in the DOM and stays where it was on the screen (realm-map.css: the host is the whole viewport and takes no pointer events). Blazor never diffs the
   children the script adds, because Razor renders none. *@
<div class="realm-map-controls"></div>
